{
  "body" : "You are designing a high-contrast monochrome character sketch with a dynamic and emotional focus.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n\n* Character: {{character}}\n* Emotion: {{emotion}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n\n* Genre / medium: High-contrast monochrome digital sketch\n* Composition: Portrait orientation with a close-up framing; subject occupies the majority of the frame, with minimal negative space\n* Lens / camera: Eye-level perspective with slight asymmetry for dynamic energy\n* Lighting: Simulated harsh lighting, creating bold contrast between black and white areas\n* Color palette and grading: Pure black lines on a white background; absence of color creates a stark, striking effect\n* Texture / surface: Visible, hand-drawn linework with rough, organic strokes\n* Post-processing: Minimal; focus on raw sketch aesthetics\n* Mood: Bold, introspective, enigmatic\n* References: Ink-style manga art, minimalist character design, traditional pen-and-ink sketches\n\nDESIGN RULES\n\n* Aspect: 3:4 portrait (~768×1024) suitable for character studies or concept art\n* Ensure the subject's face is the focal point, with attention to sharp features and expression\n* Use asymmetry in hair and facial features to create dynamic balance\n* Preserve generous visual clarity around the character; do not overcrowd the composition\n* Keep the overall image looking like an authentic artist's monochrome character sketch rather than a polished digital illustration\n\nSIGNATURE DESIGN\n\n* Add a small handwritten artist signature: \"{{signature}}\"\n* The signature must look genuinely hand-written, personal, and naturally drawn with a black ink pen\n* Use an elegant, slightly imperfect handwritten script with organic variation in stroke thickness\n* The signature should feel like the artist personally signed the original sketch\n* Place the signature near the lower-right corner, with comfortable margins from the edges\n* Keep the signature small and visually subordinate to the character\n* The signature should integrate naturally with the existing ink-sketch aesthetic\n* Treat the signature as a physical ink mark on the artwork, not as digital typography or graphic design\n* Do not add quotation marks, labels, captions, logos, watermarks, or additional text\n* The signature must remain clearly legible while retaining a natural handwritten appearance\n\nAVOID\n\n* No use of color; strictly monochrome\n* No overly detailed or hyperrealistic rendering\n* No distracting backgrounds or patterns\n* No soft or blended edges; maintain sharp, defined lines\n* No excessive shading; focus on contrast between black and white\n* No digital artifacts like pixelation\n* No typed fonts or computer-generated typography\n* No large or prominent signature\n* No signature overlapping the character's face or important facial features\n* No additional text besides the specified handwritten signature\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nCharacter: {{character}}\nEmotion: {{emotion}}\nSignature: {{signature}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}\n",
